      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "The full Theorem1.2 has negative sectional curvature and the Hadamard completeness/simply-connected setting, with constant horosphere mean curvature h>0 at one fixed ideal point. The stronger equality sigma=[h^2/4,infinity) additionally assumes negative pinching and bounded covariant derivative of curvature. Include Observation2.1, the Rellich identity and Section4 smoothness/core argument, plus Section6 cutoff/Weyl construction; the latter treats M as the trivial-group quotient. Resolvent smoothness criteria and the published geometric cutoff-Laplacian estimate [5,Section6] are explicitly established background, not missing newly claimed lemmas. The source provides the new estimate application and exact norm/error calculation. Domain and nontrivial-quotient variants are not separate counted claims."
      },
